Source: dct-os-defaults
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: DCT IT Services <it@dct.edu.ph>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dct-os-defaults
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         libglib2.0-bin,
         grub2-common,
         plymouth
Description: DCT OS identity, theme and desktop defaults
 Ships the DCT OS branding payload and applies it: /etc/os-release identity,
 GRUB theme, Plymouth splash, GLib schema overrides, Firefox policy, and the
 default user skeleton.
 .
 Branding is applied by /usr/share/dct-os/apply-branding.sh, which is
 idempotent and can be re-run at any time:
 .
   sudo /usr/share/dct-os/apply-branding.sh
 .
 This package diverts /etc/os-release (see postinst) because base-files owns
 that path and would otherwise overwrite the DCT OS identity on upgrade.
